## When working on Minkowski steps

- First make a toy version in `Experiments/` that proves:
  - symmetry (`∀ x ∈ s, -x ∈ s`)
  - convexity (`Convex ℝ s`)
  - a volume identity/bound (`volume s = ...` or `... ≤ volume s`)
  - countability of the lattice type (`[Countable ↥L]`), explicitly

## Common pitfalls (seen in this repo)

- `simp` rewriting `Set.pi ... (Icc ...)` into `Set.Icc (fun i => ...) (fun i => ...)` can break
  downstream lemmas expecting the “pi form”. Use `simp [..., -Set.pi_univ_Icc]` to keep the shape.
- `ENNReal.ofReal (p^n)` vs `(ENNReal.ofReal p)^n`: normalize using `ENNReal.ofReal_pow`.
